          ],
          "conclusion": "A Go slice is a non-copying view that shares its underlying array, but indexed slice elements are writable and slice expressions preserve the slice type. The standard language has no read-only slice/view type that prevents writes through that alias, so xs[:] does not satisfy the required non-copying read-only view.",
